<!--
  Pocket Prose's launcher icon: a closed notebook seen from above and slightly to one side, with a
  black ribbon marker laid across the cover and folded over the fore edge.

  Generated from assets/icon_mk3.svg, which is the editable source and lives beside this repository
  rather than in it. Re-export from there; do not hand-edit the path data below.

  mk3 is drawn on transparency already, so unlike mk2 there are no background rects to strip. An
  adaptive icon keeps its ground in a separate layer regardless: the tile colour lives in
  values/ic_launcher_background.xml and the two must be changed together. mk2 carried a cream
  #E9DEC7 rect that became that colour; mk3 offers no such hint, so the tile is now a decision this
  repo holds on its own rather than one inherited from the source.

  Eight paths, bottom to top: each of the two dark sheets is a #3F3839 copy sitting 2 units lower
  than the sheet itself, which shows only as a hairline along its lower edge and is what gives the
  layers a defined bottom rather than a soft fade. Then the white middle sheet, a 12% black shading
  wash across the stack, and the ribbon in two pieces — the diagonal across the cover and the
  vertical fold over the fore edge.

  There is a ninth path in the source with no fill attribute, duplicating the cover outline. SVG
  inherits fill="none" from the root there, so it draws nothing; it is dropped rather than exported
  as an opaque black shape, which is what a naive conversion produces.

  SIZE. This is the number that has been got wrong twice, so read the whole paragraph before
  changing it. The layers are 108dp, but a launcher only ever shows the **centre 72dp** — the outer
  18dp on each side is bleed for parallax and masking. So the tile you see is 72dp, not 108, and any
  scale reasoned against 108 comes out half again too big. The artwork here is 62dp wide, which is
  86% of that visible tile.

  mk1's was 58dp, 81%. This drawing is 1.35:1 against mk1's 1.2:1, so the same width buys less
  height — 58dp here left the tile looking mostly empty above and below the mark. 62 x 46.1dp fills
  it without crowding. Measured: the furthest artwork pixel sits 31.9dp from centre, inside the 33dp
  radius of the 66dp safe circle, so a round mask clips nothing. 66dp wide was rendered too and puts
  that radius at 33.9 — outside it, tips shaved — for no gain. A wide mark still needs a margin a
  square one does not, which is why this stops well short of Rubber Ring's 97%.

  CENTRING. The offsets subtract the drawing's own origin inside its canvas (63, 148) as well as
  splitting what is left over. Halving the remainder alone is not centring — it shifts the art by the
  origin, invisibly at large sizes and plainly at small ones. That bug shipped once.

  Re-measure X0/Y0/W/H by rendering the source and taking its bounding box if the artwork changes;
  they are facts about the file (63, 148, 653 x 485), not constants. mk3's underlay paths made it
  two units taller than mk2's, which is the whole of the difference between this translateY and
  mk2's — small enough to look like a typo and not one.
-->
